cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you refer to this work, cite the archived release rather than the
  repository. Each release is deposited to Zenodo and gets its own DOI; the
  concept DOI below always resolves to the newest one.
title: "districting-bench: measuring districting plans against explicit criteria"
abstract: >-
  A research system for evaluating legislative districting plans. It draws
  neutral ensembles with ReCom under a mechanically enforced firewall that keeps
  partisan and racial data out of generation, evaluates plans on many criteria at
  once without combining them into a score, builds deliberate gerrymanders to
  test detection against manufacturable ground truth, and reports three
  measurements: which criteria actually bind, whether criteria trade off against
  each other, and whether single-number fairness metrics can be gamed. Covers
  Iowa (99 counties, 4 districts) and Colorado (3,108 VTDs, 8 districts).
  Exploratory and not validated; not for litigation, advocacy, or map adoption.
type: software
